# Line endings.
#
# Every text file in this repository is stored LF — `git ls-files --eol`
# reports 185 files at `i/lf` and none at `i/crlf`. Without this file that is
# only half a policy: on Windows `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites the working copy
# to CRLF on checkout, so the working tree and the index disagree by default,
# and every `git add` of a tool-written file prints
#
#   warning: in the working copy of '<path>', LF will be replaced by CRLF
#
# Pinning `eol=lf` makes the working tree match what is actually stored, on
# every platform, whatever each contributor has set globally. The warning goes
# away because the conversion it was warning about no longer happens.
*                text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts are the one exception: PowerShell is happiest with CRLF
# and this one is never run anywhere else.
*.ps1            text eol=crlf

# Vendored assets are bytes. Declaring them stops any future `text=auto`
# misdetection from corrupting a sprite sheet or an audio file, and keeps them
# out of diffs.
*.png            binary
*.jpg            binary
*.jpeg           binary
*.gif            binary
*.ico            binary
*.ogg            binary
*.mp3            binary
*.wav            binary
*.zip            binary
*.woff           binary
*.woff2          binary
*.ttf            binary
*.otf            binary
